- How would you validate that EU masking rules are enforced without impacting non-EU tenants, and how would you test the policy at scale?
- What tracing and audit mechanisms would you implement to ensure data lineage and integrity after masking, including replay considerations?

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical end-to-end streaming with enrichment, idempotency, error handling, and observability in a beginner-friendly AWS DVA context.

## Key Concepts
- Kinesis Data Streams, Lambda enrichment, DynamoDB cache
- REST API rate-limiting handling and retries
- Idempotent S3 writes with Parquet partitioning
- DLQ, tracing (X-Ray), and LocalStack testing

## Code Example
```javascript
const AWS = require('aws-sdk');
const dynamo = new AWS.DynamoDB.DocumentClient();
const s3 = new AWS.S3();

async function enrich(event) {
  const id = event.deviceId + ':' + event.ts;
  let meta = await dynamo.get({TableName:'DeviceMeta', Key:{id}}).promise().then(r=>r.Item?.meta);
  if (!meta) {
    const resp = await fetchMetaFromApi(event.deviceId);
    meta = resp.meta;
    await dynamo.put({TableName:'DeviceMeta', Item:{id, meta}}).promise();
  }
  event.meta = meta;
  return event;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle DynamoDB cold starts or cache stampedes in this flow?
- How would you instrument LocalStack tests to validate retry/backoff and DLQ routing?

## Why This Is Asked
This question introduces Glue Schema Registry and schema evolution, a common but underrepresented real-world constraint for beginner engineers. It tests practical streaming ingestion, data validation, and basic tracing.

## Key Concepts
- Glue Schema Registry
- Backward-compatible schema
- Data enrichment from DynamoDB
- Parquet on S3 with date partition
- Kinesis Data Streams
- DLQ and observability (X-Ray)
- LocalStack testing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode for the consumer path
async function handleRecord(record){
  const valid = validateWithSchema(registry='Telemetry', version='latest', record);
  if(valid){
    const meta = await dynamo.getItem({deviceId: record.deviceId});
    const enriched = {...record, meta};
    await s3.putParquet(enriched, partitionBy='date');
  } else {
    await dlq.push(record);
  }
}
```

